# Development log

Before finishing any change, add one detailed entry at the top of `docs/DEVLOG.md`.
Skip only when the owner says not to record it. One git commit = one dated heading.

Follow the template already in that file:

- Why we chose this (and why not the alternatives)
- What changed (each behavior; files as lookup keys, not a dumped diff)
- What was affected (players, exports, database, APIs, tests, deploy)
- What we did not change
- Deploy / verification when something shipped

Do not backfill older commits unless asked. Do not invent latency, queues,
trained models, or accuracy numbers. Jaccard does not name a winning place.
